<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Margaret of Parma</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1522–1586</span> · <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Margaret of Parma was an illegitimate daughter of Emperor <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/charles-v-holy-roman-emperor">Charles V</a>. Married first to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alessandro-de-medici">Alessandro de' Medici</a> and then to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ottavio-farnese">Ottavio Farnese</a>, duke of Parma, she was governor of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/habsburg-dynasty">Habsburg</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-the-netherlands">Netherlands</a> for her half-brother Philip II from 1559 to 1567. Her rule saw growing opposition to Spanish religious policy, and she resigned after the arrival of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/fernando-alvarez-de-toledo-3rd-duke-of-alba">Duke of Alba</a>. Her son was <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alessandro-farnese-duke-of-parma">Alessandro Farnese</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/margaret-of-parma.jpg" alt="Margaret of Parma" width="320" height="450" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Antonis Mor · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Anthonis_Mor_-_Margaret,_Duchess_of_Parma_-_WGA16182.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
